ed up, and the upper bound is rounded down.\n-/\ndef div (c : Constraint) (k : Nat) : Constraint where\n  lowerBound := c.lowerBound.map fun x => (- ((- x) / k))\n  upperBound := c.upperBound.map fun y => y / k","start":193,"end":199},"axioms":[]}